From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:29:08 -0700
Subject: Do not expose pseudo-elements through LargestContentfulPaint API

If a PseudoElement is stored as the element_ in the
LargestContentfulPaint object, we would expose that to javascript
through the element attribute.

This could cause all sorts of problems, letting javascript be able to
modify them as if they were true elements, moving them around the tree
in unexpected places and setting attributes on them, for instance.

Specifically, the issue reported was modifying querySelector caches
while being traversed due to slot re-assignment.

Bug: 570638836
Change-Id: I44d87a537a7da52fa9dc2aa577a58a888c94f3de
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8545831
Commit-Queue: Scott Haseley <shaseley@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Rune Lillesveen <futhark@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Scott Haseley <shaseley@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718007}

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/largest_contentful_paint.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/largest_contentful_paint.cc
index 289f28896a6128438fe8fd6771d39143fe83c098..0e91d2fc220ce754a48cf51a76177f2516a575b5 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/largest_contentful_paint.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/largest_contentful_paint.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_object_builder.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/performance_entry_names.h"
+#include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/timing/performance.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/text/atomic_string.h"
 
 namespace blink {
@@ -43,8 +44,9 @@ PerformanceEntryType LargestContentfulPaint::EntryTypeEnum() const {
 }
 
 Element* LargestContentfulPaint::element() const {
-  if (!element_ || !element_->isConnected() || element_->IsInShadowTree())
+  if (!Performance::CanExposeNode(element_)) {
     return nullptr;
+  }
 
   // Do not expose |element_| when the document is not 'fully active'.
   const Document& document = element_->GetDocument();
